# Reach the Mnemonic Debugger on the serial console and boot the SR10.4
# cartridge from it. The cartridge counterpart of `tools/md-shell.script`, which
# takes the same route to the same prompt and then says `DI W` for the
# Winchester where this says `DI C` for the cartridge.
#
# `DI C` selects the boot device; `EX DOMAIN_OS` then loads the **tape's**
# SYSBOOT -- 1.1 MB at `01002000`, entry `01002024`. `DOMAIN_OS` is not a PROM
# command and appears nowhere in the PROM image; it is a name on the cartridge.
#
# **`>` is MD's prompt, not the PROM's**, and that is the thing to know before
# reconstructing this dialogue. The PROM never prints it: left alone, a
# disk-less machine runs its self test, prints `Could not load /SAU7/SELF_TEST.`
# and sits at PC `78E` for as long as it is given -- 1.2 G instructions, in the
# run that established this. `78E` is exactly the address `--boot-input-after-pc`
# holds the knock for, so a machine "stuck" there is a machine waiting to be
# knocked at.
#
# The banner-then-prompt rule is `md-shell.script`'s and applies unchanged: MD
# prints `\r\n>` *after* its sign-on and discards what is typed while it is
# still printing, so waiting on the banner alone loses the first character.
expect MD7C
expect >
send DI C\r
expect >
send EX DOMAIN_OS\r
